  ],
  "lines": [
    {
      "index": 0,
      "kind": "narration",
      "speaker": "john_watson",
      "text": "Lestrade's news knocked the whiskey clean out of Gregson's hand, and nobody spoke.",
      "shot": 0,
      "at": 0.25,
      "seconds": 5.82
    },
    {
      "index": 1,
      "kind": "dialogue",
      "speaker": "sherlock_holmes",
      "text": "Stangerson too. The plot thickens.",
      "shot": 1,
      "at": 6.583,
      "seconds": 2.5
    },
    {
      "index": 2,
      "kind": "narration",
      "speaker": "john_watson",
      "text": "He had reached Halliday's Private Hotel at eight that morning and asked after Joseph Stangerson.",
      "shot": 2,
      "at": 9.583,
      "seconds": 5.88
    },
    {
      "index": 3,
      "kind": "dialogue",
      "speaker": "g_lestrade",
      "text": "He is upstairs in bed. He wished to be called at nine.",
      "shot": 3,
      "at": 16.0,
      "seconds": 3.56
    },
    {
      "index": 4,
      "kind": "narration",
      "speaker": "john_watson",
      "text": "From under the door a thin red ribbon had crept out across the passage.",
      "shot": 5,
      "at": 22.083,
      "seconds": 4.36
    },
    {
      "index": 5,
      "kind": "narration",
      "speaker": "john_watson",
      "text": "The door was locked upon the inside, so the two of them put their shoulders to it.",
      "shot": 6,
      "at": 26.958,
      "seconds": 4.8
    },
    {
      "index": 6,
      "kind": "narration",
      "speaker": "john_watson",
      "text": "The window stood wide open, and the man lay huddled beneath the sill in his nightdress.",
      "shot": 7,
      "at": 32.292,
      "seconds": 5.92
    },
    {
      "index": 7,
      "kind": "narration",
      "speaker": "john_watson",
      "text": "Cold, and some hours dead.",
      "shot": 8,
      "at": 38.75,
      "seconds": 2.8
    },
    {
      "index": 8,
      "kind": "narration",
      "speaker": "john_watson",
      "text": "One deep stab in the left side. And above the bed, in dried blood, that word again.",
      "shot": 9,
      "at": 42.083,
      "seconds": 7.0
    },
    {
      "index": 9,
      "kind": "narration",
      "speaker": "john_watson",
      "text": "A milk boy passing the lane at first light had seen a ladder raised to that window.",
      "shot": 10,
      "at": 49.583,
      "seconds": 5.16
    },
    {
      "index": 10,
      "kind": "narration",
      "speaker": "john_watson",
      "text": "A tall man in a long brown coat came down it and walked away without hurrying.",
      "shot": 11,
      "at": 55.25,
      "seconds": 5.1
    },
    {
      "index": 11,
      "kind": "narration",
      "speaker": "john_watson",
      "text": "He had stayed to wash his hands in the basin, and had wiped his knife upon the sheets.",
      "shot": 12,
      "at": 60.875,
      "seconds": 5.8
    },
    {
      "index": 12,
      "kind": "dialogue",
      "speaker": "sherlock_holmes",
      "text": "The last link. My case is complete.",
      "shot": 13,
      "at": 67.208,
      "seconds": 2.61
    },
    {
      "index": 13,
      "kind": "narration",
      "speaker": "john_watson",
      "text": "He asked me to fetch up the old terrier our landlady had wanted put out of its pain.",
      "shot": 14,
      "at": 70.333,
      "seconds": 5.3
    },
    {
      "index": 14,
      "kind": "narration",
      "speaker": "john_watson",
      "text": "He cut one of the pills in two, dissolved a half in water, and added a little milk.",
      "shot": 15,
      "at": 76.167,
      "seconds": 5.24
    },
    {
      "index": 15,
      "kind": "narration",
      "speaker": "john_watson",
      "text": "The dog licked the saucer dry.",
      "shot": 16,
      "at": 81.917,
      "seconds": 2.49
    },
    {
      "index": 16,
      "kind": "narration",
      "speaker": "john_watson",
      "text": "He stood over it with his watch open in his hand.",
      "shot": 17,
      "at": 84.917,
      "seconds": 3.49
    },
    {
      "index": 17,
      "kind": "narration",
      "speaker": "john_watson",
      "text": "Nothing happened. Minute followed minute, and the two detectives began to enjoy themselves.",
      "shot": 18,
      "at": 90.417,
      "seconds": 6.1
    },
    {
      "index": 18,
      "kind": "narration",
      "speaker": "john_watson",
      "text": "Then he gave a shriek of delight, went at the box again, and cut the second pill.",
      "shot": 19,
      "at": 97.042,
      "seconds": 5.6
    },
    {
      "index": 19,
      "kind": "narration",
      "speaker": "john_watson",
      "text": "One shiver, and it was over.",
      "shot": 20,
      "at": 103.167,
      "seconds": 1.97
    },
    {
      "index": 20,
      "kind": "dialogue",
      "speaker": "sherlock_holmes",
      "text": "Of the two, one was the deadliest poison and the other was nothing at all.",
      "shot": 21,
      "at": 105.667,
      "seconds": 4.06
    },
    {
      "index": 21,
      "kind": "narration",
      "speaker": "john_watson",
      "text": "A tap at the door, and Wiggins put his head in to say the cab had come.",
      "shot": 22,
      "at": 110.25,
      "seconds": 4.28
    },
    {
      "index": 22,
      "kind": "narration",
      "speaker": "john_watson",
      "text": "Holmes knelt over a portmanteau he had never mentioned, and asked the driver for a hand.",
      "shot": 23,
      "at": 115.042,
      "seconds": 5.64
    },
    {
      "index": 23,
      "kind": "dialogue",
      "speaker": "g_lestrade",
      "text": "The old pattern is good enough, if we can only find the man to put them on.",
      "shot": 24,
      "at": 122.417,
      "seconds": 3.83
    }
  ]
}